# Terraform AWS Route Table Association Module

Terraform module to associate an AWS subnet with an AWS route table.

## Architecture

```text
Subnet
   │
   │ association
   ▼
Route Table
```

This module only manages the association between an existing subnet and an existing route table.

## Usage

```hcl
module "route_table_association" {
  source = "github.com/IndrajitRajasooriar/terraform-modules//modules/route_table_association?ref=main"

  subnet_id      = module.subnet.subnet_id
  route_table_id = module.route_table.route_table_id
}
```

## Inputs

| Name             | Type     | Required | Description                                         |
| ---------------- | -------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
| `subnet_id`      | `string` | Yes      | ID of the subnet to associate with the route table. |
| `route_table_id` | `string` | Yes      | ID of the route table to associate with the subnet. |

## Outputs

| Name                         | Description                        |
| ---------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| `route_table_association_id` | ID of the route table association. |

## Resources

This module creates:

* `aws_route_table_association`

## Example

```hcl
module "route_table_association_1" {
  source = "github.com/IndrajitRajasooriar/terraform-modules//modules/route_table_association?ref=main"

  subnet_id      = module.subnet_1.subnet_id
  route_table_id = module.route_table_1.route_table_id
}
```

## Notes

This module does not create:

* VPCs
* Subnets
* Route tables
* Routes
* Internet Gateways
* NAT Gateways

Those resources should be managed by their respective modules.

The route table itself is responsible for defining routes such as:

```text
10.1.0.0/16 → VPC Peering Connection
0.0.0.0/0   → Internet Gateway
```

The association simply determines which route table is used by the subnet.
